John H. wrote:
> 1. Blessed +2 gray dragon scale mail.  (Dragon scale is the best armor,
> and this way I get the best intrinsic.)
[SNIP SDSM]
> 3. Blessed fireproof +2 boots of speed.  (For permanent intrinsic
> speed.  Speed is not necessary, but it is a very useful intrinsic.)

In the early and late game, jumping is a better choice IMO (assuming
you've gotten basic speed from somewhere, like role-based, a wand, or a
quantum mechanic).  You can get away from things a lot faster, kill
them from range, and cross traps/Medusa/etc.

> 4. Blessed bag of holding (if one is not averse to Sokoban it's best to
> check there first)

Not worth a pre-castle wish at all.  It's really not needed to ascend,
but it's very convenient; I'll wish one up at the castle (since I
rarely use all the wishes there anyway) but before then I'm
concentrating on things that help my survivability a lot more than the
bag.

> 12. Cloak of displacement (Middling cancellation, and only if magic
> resistance is GDSM-derived, but this can be a fun item.)

I'd go with the following (although artifact wishes would change it,
and if it's a wand then blessed ?charging comes first if I've not found
them--I'll often hold off on using the wand until it's ID'd and not use
the 0:1 wish until I find ?charging if I'm pretty well set up already)
1. Gray/silver DSM (gray unless you have MR)
2. Reflection source (amulet)
3. Jumping boots
4. Magic marker (if I don't have any)
5. =conflict, =teleport control, or ?genocide (if it's getting deepish
and I've not found any yet, depending on what I already have and what
my needs are)

Things I would rarely wish for that appear on a lot of wishing
spoilers:
1. Gauntlets of power.  I prefer leather gloves or dex; for pure
wombats these are nice but they've got good str already so rarely worth
a wish, I could _maybe_ see a barb going for them if he's really well
equipped already. A pre-Quest valk would do better wishing up a blessed
tinning kit--I'm too conservative to ever risk throwing Mjollnir.
2. Speed boots. I _might_ go for these if I'm pretty well kitted out
and about to wander through Gehennom, where jumping is less useful.
Probably not.
3. Amulet of life saving.  I prefer "oR and a good cloak (robe,
oilskin) or CoMR and "oESP.
4. Artifact weapons.  I'll settle for a couple non-artifact sabers if I
must, but usually you get something good from saccing a couple times.
5. Cloak of disp.  MC2 scares me.
6. =slow digestion.  Unless you're planning a long altar-camping
munchkinfest, food won't be a problem once you're past the first few
levels of the dungeon.  If I'm still that early,  GDSM is  still better
odds.



